---
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
import CalloutBlock from "@plugdash/callout/Callout.astro";
import InstallCommand from "../../components/InstallCommand.astro";
import PluginReference from "../../components/PluginReference.astro";
import { pluginDocToc } from "../../data/doc-toc";
import { getPlugin } from "../../data/plugins";
import Doc from "../../layouts/Doc.astro";

const plugin = getPlugin("callout")!;
---

<Doc
  tocEntries={pluginDocToc}
  currentSlug="callout"
  title="callout"
  section="@plugdash/callout"
  description="Info, warning, tip, and danger blocks for the EmDash editor."
>
  <h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>
  <p>
    Registers a <code>callout</code> block type in the EmDash Portable
    Text editor. Authors type <code>/</code>, pick Callout, choose one of
    four variants (info, warning, tip, danger) and add an optional title.
    <code>Callout.astro</code> is wired into EmDash's PortableText
    renderer automatically, so callouts show on your site with no theme
    code. The plugin declares no capabilities and stores nothing outside
    the post.
  </p>
  <p>
    callout is a Native plugin, because it ships an Astro block renderer.
  </p>

  <CalloutBlock variant="tip" title="Tip" body="Use the tip variant for the non-obvious thing that makes a task easier. This block is the plugin rendering itself on its own doc page." />

  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <InstallCommand command={plugin.installCommand} />

  <h2 id="register">Register</h2>
  <p>
    Open <code>astro.config.mjs</code> at the root of your Astro project.
    Import the plugin at the top, then add it to the <code>plugins</code>
    array of the <code>emdash()</code> integration - the one that sits
    inside Astro's top-level <code>integrations</code> array:
  </p>
  <Code language="js" filename="astro.config.mjs" code={`import { defineConfig } from "astro/config"
import emdash from "emdash/astro"
import { calloutPlugin } from "@plugdash/callout"

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [
    emdash({
      plugins: [calloutPlugin()],
    }),
  ],
})`} />

  <h2 id="add-the-component">Add the component</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing to add for callouts written in the editor: EmDash renders them
    with <code>Callout.astro</code> on its own. To use one by hand in a
    page, pass the text as <code>body</code>. A blank line starts a new
    paragraph. Without <code>body</code> the component renders nothing.
  </p>
  <Code language="astro" code={`---
import Callout from "@plugdash/callout/Callout.astro"
---
<Callout variant="info" title="Heads up" body="Content goes here." />`} />

  <h2 id="live-demo">Live demo</h2>
  <div class="demo-inline" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.75rem">
    <CalloutBlock variant="info" title="Info" body="Background context readers might want but don't strictly need." />
    <CalloutBlock variant="warning" title="Warning" body="Something that will bite them if they skip it." />
    <CalloutBlock variant="danger" title="Danger" body="Something that will break things if they get it wrong." />
  </div>

  <PluginReference plugin={plugin} />

  <h2 id="for-agents">For agents</h2>
  <p>After installing @plugdash/callout and registering
  <code>calloutPlugin()</code>, open a post in the EmDash editor, type
  <code>/</code> and confirm Callout is in the block menu. Add one, save,
  and check it renders on the page. No layout change is needed. Data
  stored: the callout block inside the post's Portable Text.</p>
</Doc>
